course: dictionary
lesson: 6515
title: Neither: not this one and not that one
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Neither means not one and not the other, when you are talking about two things. «Which one? Neither!» means the speaker wants neither of the two choices.
explain: Use neither in pairs with nor. «Neither tea nor milk» means no tea and no milk. Both things are not true.
explain: You can also use neither to agree with someone who says no. «I don't like spinach.» «Me neither.» means I also do not like it.
explain: Christina Rossetti wrote, «Who has seen the wind? / Neither I nor you». The poem says that neither the speaker nor the reader has seen the wind. Context shows you what neither means.
fact: Neither means not one, and not the other, when there are two things.
fact: «Neither ... nor» joins two things that are both not true, as in «neither tea nor milk».
fact: «Me neither» means I also do not.
fact: In maths sorting problems, neither means not in either group. In «At least one: 14 + 12 - 5 = 21, neither: 30 - 21 = 9», nine people are in neither group.
exercise: Ali is asked, «Which one? Neither!» What does Ali mean? | The first one only | *Not this one and not that one | Both of them together | He cannot count
exercise: Mia says, «I don't like peas.» Ben replies, «Me ___.» Which word fits the gap? | ever | always | both | *neither
exercise: What does «neither tea nor milk» mean? | Only tea | Milk, but warm | *No tea and no milk | Tea and milk together
test: Which word completes this sentence? «Neither Sara ___ Tom came to the party.» | but | or | *nor | and
test: In a Venn diagram, what is the neither part? | Things in both circles | Things in the first circle only | *Things outside both circles | The line in the middle
exam: Mum asks, «Tea or juice?» Dad says, «Neither, thanks.» What does Dad mean? | He wants only juice | He wants both tea and juice | He wants only tea | *He wants no tea and no juice
